From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Filippo Falezza <filippo.falezza@outlook.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 19:38:56 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 122/159] remoteproc: qcom: pas: Print auth error code

"failed to authenticate image and release reset" does not say why.
Include the error returned by qcom_scm_pas_auth_and_reset(), which
tells a firmware rejection apart from a failure of the SCM call.

This patch was generated by an AI coding assistant (Claude Opus 5.5 in
Claude Code) during an interactive bring-up session on a Motorola Moto G
5G Plus (XT2075-3, "nairo"). It has not yet been reviewed line by line
by a human and needs that review before any submission.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Filippo Falezza <filippo.falezza@outlook.com>
---
 drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5_pas.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5_pas.c b/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5_pas.c
index 88b4e252080b..c8063cfc6131 100644
--- a/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5_pas.c
+++ b/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5_pas.c
@@ -365,7 +365,7 @@ static int qcom_pas_start(struct rproc *rproc)
 	ret = qcom_pas_prepare_and_auth_reset(pas->pas_ctx);
 	if (ret) {
 		dev_err(pas->dev,
-			"failed to authenticate image and release reset\n");
+			"failed to authenticate image and release reset: %d\n", ret);
 		goto unmap_carveout;
 	}
 
